1
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,897
You're officially under
ship arrest, captain!

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:18,417
Sorry, I...

3
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,757
I moved on.

4
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,457
You did more than that, you idiot!

5
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,658
You could've killed your whole crew!

6
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:31,820
How can you be so stupid?

7
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:40,500
Well, we all made it out
all right, didn't we?

8
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:41,997
That's all that matters.

9
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:42,940
What was that?

10
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,920
Are you going easy on him, Jinbei?

11
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:50,640
Is that Conqueror's Haki?

12
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,600
It's not worth it, boss.

13
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,017
Back away, soldier.

14
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,571
You're in the blast zone.

15
00:00:58,040 --> 00:00:58,870
All done?

16
00:00:58,953 --> 00:01:00,861
You patched things up so quickly.

17
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:04,480
Yep, thanks to the Sunny. She's tough.

18
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,677
Took that fall like a total champ.

19
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:08,237
Only broke a yard in fact.

20
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,202
Not too shabby.

21
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:12,285
Captain sure put her
through her paces, though.

22
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,380
Robin, dear!

23
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:20,080
Your snack is here.

24
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:23,000
Why, thank you.

25
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:28,370
Oh.

26
00:01:28,453 --> 00:01:29,620
Her wanted posters.

27
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:30,901
They're all new.

28
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:36,440
Wanted posters?

29
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:38,260
Can I see?

30
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:52,680
An emperor of the sea and the senior
captain of the Straw Hat fleet.

31
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,697
Straw Hat Luffy and his
nine crewmates are now some

32
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:58,597
of the most important players
in the world of Pirates.

33
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,680
It's only natural that
their bounties would change.

34
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,180
Did it go up?

35
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:20,117
The ship's doctor, cotton candy
lover, Chopper, listed as a pet.

36
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:22,377
Bounty, 1,000 berries.

37
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:24,600
Up by 900 berries.

38
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:26,530
Hey!

39
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:29,080
Is this some kind of joke?

40
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,590
Huh?

41
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,640
Navigator, Cat, Burglar, Nami.

42
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,400
Bounty, 366 million berries.

43
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,430
Why?

44
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,440
Why can't I have that money?

45
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:53,100
Yo-ho-ho, yo-ho!

46
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,140
Yeah, baby!

47
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:01,220
Musician Soul King Brooke.

48
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:06,000
Bounty, 383 million berries. Thank you!

49
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,440
What?

50
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:15,240
Shipwright, Cyborg Franky.

51
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:18,720
Bounty, 394 million berries.

52
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,760
Those government bastards!

53
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:23,360
Where the hell am I?

54
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:34,440
Sniper, God Usopp.

55
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:37,060
Bounty, 500 million berries.

56
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:38,990
Enough!

57
00:03:39,073 --> 00:03:40,900
I don't want it to go up anymore!

58
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,780
This should cheer you up.

59
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:44,940
Don't be sad.

60
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:53,840
Archaeologist, demon child, Nico
Robin, bounty, 930 million berries.

61
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:08,937
Cook, blackleg Sanji, bounty,
1 billion 32 million berries.

62
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:11,500
Jinbei, here's yours!

63
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:15,177
Oh, you were kicking ass back there.

64
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,613
You made quite a scene.

65
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:26,075
Elmsman, first son of the sea, Jinbei.

66
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:29,040
Bounty, 1,100,000,000 berries.

67
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:33,564
Swordsman, pirate hunter, Zoro.

68
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,080
Bounty, 1,111,000,000 berries.

69
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,710
Damn it!

70
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:40,160
I'm lower than him?

71
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,260
But how?

72
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:43,220
Are you all right, Sanji?

73
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,580
You seem troubled.

74
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:48,000
I do not need any
sympathy from you, Jinbae.

75
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,360
You're both dead to me. Huh?

76
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:52,740
Nah, he's fine. Ignore him.

77
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,334
He's just mad because he's number four.

78
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,800
What the hell did you call me?

79
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:04,280
Just restrict the second,
please. Calm down.

80
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,200
I won't do it again.

81
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,649
Please let me out of here.

82
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:15,680
Senior captain and an emperor
of the sea, Straw Hat Luffy.

83
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:18,240
Bounty, three billion berries.

84
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,100
I'm so hungry.

85
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,940
Did you see?

86
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:28,357
Yeah, that was crazy.

87
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:30,620
It was really them! No way!

88
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:36,365
They call the world's
greatest torch, you know?

89
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:38,200
Outstairs! So cool!

90
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:43,557
I thought we were finished when the Navy

91
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,737
shut down the warlords
and came for our necks.

92
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:48,200
But somehow, we're still here.

93
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:51,020
We've got Buggy to think for that.

94
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:53,020
Our chairman is the best.

95
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:58,880
Please spare me!

96
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:04,080
You can take whatever you want
from here, just let me go!

97
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,380
Hey, thank you.

98
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,120
Come on, I'll do anything you say.

99
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:13,152
I'll lick your boots, just don't kill me!

100
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:21,317
You know, when Hawkeye and I found it,

101
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:24,106
Crossgill, we were hoping
to run it ourselves.

102
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,300
So tell me something, Back.

103
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,300
Why are you the boss?

104
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:32,266
Well, I mean, all I can
say is I'm real sorry.

105
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:34,342
I'll have better luck next time.

106
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:37,737
And that's all it takes to
be an emperor of the sea?

107
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:40,114
Some crying and a half-hearted apology?

108
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,959
Frankly, it sets a bad
example if we keep you alive.

109
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:47,940
This is more than just humiliation.

110
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:52,326
A thousand deaths wouldn't pay
back the insult you've dealt me.

111
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:55,620
I'd rather you just die.

112
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:03,915
Well, look who it is!

113
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,200
Hello, boss.

114
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:08,157
Why, this is just like the
good old days, isn't it?

115
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,900
It would be so nice working for you again.

116
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:13,820
You worm stabbing me in the back.

117
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:16,100
Hug Aldino! Am I?

118
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:20,114
Because I don't recall becoming
your subordinate, buggy.

119
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:23,800
Two-faced little prick.

120
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,740
Go ahead.

121
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:27,469
Call me whatever you like.

122
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:31,520
Well, the chairman is dead. So what now?

123
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:32,777
You guys got a plan?

124
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,117
I'm happy to serve, crocodile.

125
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:39,720
Well, this is a dog-eat-dog
world we live in.

126
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:44,660
Seems you pushed your
luck, buggy boy! Dammit!

127
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:47,200
I'm gonna bite your finger off!

128
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:55,017
I hear you've lost your privilege
as a warlord of the sea, Miyok.

129
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:56,460
And what is your point?

130
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,856
I'd make it quickly.

131
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:02,080
As you may know, this island is
surrounded by the Navy right now.

132
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:03,200
They move fast.

133
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:07,617
Typical of the world
government to put together a

134
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,157
little committee just to pull
the rug out from under you.

135
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:13,652
I'm sure they were all proud
of themselves at the reverie.

136
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,317
But that's that.

137
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,817
Now you're nothing but
a filthy pirate to them.

138
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:21,606
They can't wait to cut you down
if it'll make them look better.

139
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:24,537
You set them on the road to this yourself.

140
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:25,737
Mind your tongue.

141
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:27,840
That was a long time ago.

142
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,437
If you're quite finished.

143
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:34,017
I have a rather urgent move to make.

144
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:36,500
Good, then why not come here?

145
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:40,100
You don't have a better plan, do you?

146
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:46,000
If we team up together, we can form an
organization the Navy will have to respect.

147
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:50,340
You were known as the Marine
Hunter once upon a time.

148
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,697
Neither of us trust other people.

149
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:55,015
We have that much in common, at least.

150
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:57,740
It's not a bad deal, Hawkeye.

151
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,634
What's with that look?

152
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:06,819
What does he want?

153
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:09,620
Why do bad things always happen to me?

154
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:11,680
I've never done a thing wrong!

155
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,300
You gotta come quick!

156
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:17,200
Stop your crying! Go out and fight!

157
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:19,834
You're not scared of the Navy, are you?

158
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:21,860
Buzz off!

159
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,057
I'm trying to sneak away
here and you're ruining it!

160
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:27,077
Somebody's attacking the Navy ships!

161
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:28,984
Look, they're all getting sunk!

162
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,300
It's a massacre out there!

163
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:36,720
But who would help us?

164
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,880
This is scary!

165
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,220
They're so strong!

166
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:46,960
It's Crocodile!

167
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:56,060
Get bossed!

168
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:03,300
Open fire!

169
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:21,000
I heard rumors that Crocodile
is Captain Buggy's henchmen.

170
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:22,600
I guess they're true.

171
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:25,920
His prettiest life on the
line to rescue all of us.

172
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:28,100
All thanks to Chairman Buggy!

173
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,440
That's right.

174
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,760
Just as I planned. ...pens.

175
00:10:37,380 --> 00:10:40,820
He bored my ass out before and
now he's coming to collect!

176
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,797
I don't have that kind of money!

177
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:45,077
Why do you think I was borrowing from you?

178
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,960
I'd rather face the Navy!

179
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:54,168
Surprised you stuck around.

180
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:56,460
I thought you'd make a run for it.

181
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,980
I was trying to!

182
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:02,608
Funny thing about business.

183
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,157
It looks like I'm doing well, but
there's just so much overhead,

184
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,860
so many mouths to feed.

185
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:11,957
Also, my biggest earners were the
giants, and they all walked out.

186
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,680
Oh, so you can't pay.

187
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:15,296
Slavery it is, then.

188
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,891
We'll sell you off today.

189
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:19,360
Come on, Krieg baby.

190
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,757
We broke out of Impale Town together.

191
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:22,781
What about that?

192
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:24,700
We're impals, right?

193
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:27,977
Why do you think I lent you
the money in the first place?

194
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:29,680
But that debt's been paid.

195
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:31,817
Time for you to hold up your end.

196
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,377
Yeah, but...

197
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,048
I've got a company to fund.

198
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,966
Now, are you gonna pay
what you owe me or not?

199
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,420
Relax, okay?

200
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:45,637
I've got tons of experience.

201
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,217
I'll help you run your business.

202
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:49,640
I'm a former warlord of the sea, too.

203
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:52,020
We'll make a perfect team.

204
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:53,730
Really?

205
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:56,660
I'll work off every last berry I owe.

206
00:11:56,980 --> 00:12:01,320
For starters, I'll give your
company one hell of a classy debut.

207
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:04,680
I've got human resources at the wazoo!

208
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,520
Advertising, printing, transportation!

209
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,940
All at your fingertips!

210
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,478
And the work is free of charge, too!

211
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:17,780
So, your genius idea for a flyer was this?

212
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:23,040
I can't help but notice
you're at the top, President.

213
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,380
No, wait a sec.

214
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:28,300
That was an accident, I promise you!

215
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:30,240
Well, so is this.

216
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:39,460
Listen, I swear that wasn't my intention.

217
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:41,566
This is all my staff's fault.

218
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:44,013
They worship the ground I walk on, okay?

219
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:46,220
It took me by surprise, too.

220
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:50,260
Look at the poster I made.

221
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:51,400
It's cool.

222
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,680
It's cool, right?

223
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:54,620
Damn it.

224
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:55,781
What did you do?

225
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:59,416
I made you look extra awesome
because you're the best.

226
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:06,428
You haven't shown this
to anyone yet, right?

227
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,420
Nobody important, boss.

228
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:10,601
Just everyone in the whole world.

229
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,360
As I'm sure you've heard,

230
00:13:20,540 --> 00:13:23,537
Buggy was the mastermind behind
the Impel Down prison break.

231
00:13:23,620 --> 00:13:26,200
He was even on Roger's crew years ago.

232
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:30,955
He and Redhead Shanks have quite a
bit of history, so he's no small fry.

233
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,730
Also,

234
00:13:32,813 --> 00:13:34,837
he's so well-liked among
pirates that Crocodile

235
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:37,437
came to his aid when we
attacked Empty Bluffs Island.

236
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:40,997
The partnership between Crocodile
and Mihawk was no surprise, though.

237
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:43,315
We confirmed that through wiretapping.

238
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:47,797
Shady organizations are already
investing in their marine hunting.

239
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:51,457
We're seeing a rise in insurgency
all over the world right now.

240
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:53,197
Cross Guild is feeding into it.

241
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:55,557
We should consider them
a significant threat.

242
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:58,405
What are the bounties on
Cross Guild's members?

243
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,920
First up, the former warlord of the sea,

244
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:06,937
Sir Crocodile His logia-type Devil Fruit
power is still formidable He also has

245
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:13,980
a strong intellect and leadership skills
His bounty is 1,965,000,000 berries Then,

246
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:17,297
Hawkeye Mihawk The former
warlord is hailed as

247
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:19,937
the world's greatest swordsman
Even above red-haired

248
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:23,297
shanks A man with
extraordinary strength deserves

249
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:27,920
an extraordinary bounty
3,590,000,000 berries.

250
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:31,700
Lastly, there's Buggy the Genius Jester.

251
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:34,320
We spoke about his storied history.

252
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:38,560
But more than that, he commands
the power of the other two men.

253
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:43,160
So his bounty is 3,189,000,000 berries.

254
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:47,540
Just like Straw Hat Luffy, we
consider him to be a new emperor.

255
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:52,000
In other words, he is a threat
to the world government itself.

256
00:14:53,660 --> 00:15:00,317
Look at you, an emperor—that's
quite the achievement for a clown!

257
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,797
That's enough,

258
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:08,677
you know;

259
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:12,217
this might work out in our
favor, don't you think?

260
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:14,337
He'd be useful as a
figurehead for the guild.

261
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:20,337
I have no interest in becoming an
emperor; I'd much rather live in peace.

262
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:23,244
peace and let him carry
that target on his back.

263
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:24,440
You serious?

264
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:27,357
We might as well let him
take the heat for a while.

265
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:30,028
And if we change our
minds, we can kill him.

266
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,280
Fine by me.

267
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:48,280
Our time is now!

268
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:50,130
This era!

269
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:52,997
will require a new vision and new leaders

270
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:56,060
we founded cross guild
to seize its reigns.

271
00:15:56,780 --> 00:16:03,360
allow me to introduce our
executives first up sir crocodile.

272
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:12,060
and next the great swordsman hawk guy.

273
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:22,074
Looks like we're back.

274
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,610
Fools!

275
00:16:23,693 --> 00:16:24,523
You're the best!

276
00:16:24,606 --> 00:16:27,260
We do it right, and do it flashy!

277
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:29,340
What do you say?

278
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:36,170
Look!

279
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:38,340
He's shedding tears of joy!

280
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:39,977
Oh, Tang it, I'll...

281
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:42,380
I'm gonna start crashing tears!

282
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:46,600
I've lost control of my ride!

283
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:56,700
I see it, Marco. We're here.

284
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:58,090
Yeah?

285
00:16:58,460 --> 00:17:00,460
All right, I'll be taking off now.

286
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:05,200
Thanks for the ride. It was fun.

287
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:06,420
Bye, Shanks.

288
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:07,882
You're leaving?

289
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:10,417
You sure you don't want
to join my crew, Marco?

290
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:11,330
Come on.

291
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:14,580
Thanks, but no thanks.

292
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,157
You big-shot pirates are too much.

293
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:25,037
No more babysitting for
me, give me a break!

294
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:26,897
I'm not that high maintenance.

295
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,857
Tell them back—you want me to lie?

296
00:17:28,940 --> 00:17:29,770
See

297
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:34,970
ya!

298
00:17:35,053 --> 00:17:35,883
What

299
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:53,657
you're not gonna come with us—we
were gonna be pirates together!

300
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:54,860
You felt

301
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:09,897
what happened back there, didn't you?

302
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:15,277
When that woodsman attacked, we were on
the verge of defeat. When someone's Haki.

303
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,190
someone's Haki

304
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:17,690
saved this country.

305
00:18:17,773 --> 00:18:20,584
Kaido is gone, but other
enemies will target us.

306
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:22,860
And now that I know that...

307
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:26,060
I'd go crazy if I left!

308
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:30,297
I can't have a fun adventure while
I'm worried about my friends at home.

309
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:32,204
You'd feel the same way, right?

310
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:34,969
But I still want to be
a part of your crew!

311
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:36,700
Make me an honorary member!

312
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:40,220
I guess I understand.

313
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:48,520
That might be good, actually.

314
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:52,834
If you stay in the land of
Wano, it'll be in good hands.

315
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,435
I'll leave it to you.

316
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:57,800
Keep Momo safe.

317
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:02,780
It won't be easy.

318
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,120
Momo has a lot of pride, you know.

319
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:07,640
He might be stubborn. I am too.

320
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,137
Don't worry about me.

321
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:10,279
I can handle this.

322
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,620
Yamato, no.

323
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,660
Hey, Straw Hat!

324
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,260
Hey, Marco!

325
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:22,457
There's a ship nearby that's
going my way, so I'm taking off.

326
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:24,128
It's been a real adventure.

327
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:25,180
Sure has.

328
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:27,020
Have a safe trip! You too.

329
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:31,160
I wanted to ask.

330
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:32,640
Back in Marineford.

331
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:35,528
You saved my life during
that battle, right?

332
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:38,880
Carry Straw Hat if you won't run! Hurry!

333
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:40,420
Thanks for that.

334
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,177
Everyone was working hard to save you.

335
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:45,820
Jinbei 2, why was that?

336
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,540
Oh, well, it's been quite a while.

337
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:49,978
It's, uh, I recall.

338
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:55,620
You've come a long way since then.

339
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:58,153
I'm sure Ace would be real proud of you.

340
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:04,640
I sure hope so.

341
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:12,840
Luffy, this age belongs to you now.

342
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:15,500
Better take good care of it.

343
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:20,030
Right.

344
00:20:20,113 --> 00:20:20,943
See ya!

345
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:36,980
Please, sweetie, don't
be so hard on yourself.

346
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:38,180
He's fine.

347
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:41,180
It's Sabo.

348
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:42,812
He'll make it back soon.

349
00:20:43,260 --> 00:20:44,090
Right.

350
00:20:44,173 --> 00:20:47,057
On the bright side, at least
everyone survived the mission.

351
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:48,240
There you go!

352
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:51,060
We have to celebrate every little miracle!

353
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,460
Yee-haw!

354
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:56,440
But golly gee, that darn Sabo!

355
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:58,780
How dare he make us worry so much!

356
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:01,194
My little heart can't take all of this!

357
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:05,362
I wish I knew what happened, but
we were already split up by then.

358
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,540
Still, I believe in Sabo.

359
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:08,940
Hey, that's my line!

360
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,877
I believed in Sabo way before you did!

361
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:13,260
In fact, my hopes for him are, Skye...

362
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,180
Would you shut up?

363
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:21,400
We're an army, not a dance circus.

364
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:33,710
Dragon.

365
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:39,140
Sabo will be all right.

366
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:47,280
However, if he really killed King Cobra,
that's not something I can ever approve of.

367
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:50,080
It doesn't matter what the reason is.

368
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:52,340
It's unacceptable.

369
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:05,300
Now, Kuma, we've done enough speculating.

370
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,800
Why don't you tell me what you saw?

371
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:14,600
As you wish, master.

372
00:22:15,920 --> 00:22:19,200
As you wish.

373
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:41,340
We've got an incoming call
to the Kamabaka Queendom.

374
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:43,385
It could be the Flame Emperor.

375
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:47,040
Trace it and record the call. Yes, sir.

376
00:22:57,700 --> 00:22:58,537
Badapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadapadu.

377
00:22:58,620 --> 00:22:59,480
Kolic.

378
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:02,530
Hello?

379
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,300
This is Koala.

380
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:07,060
It's me.

381
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:10,020
It's Sabo.

382
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,380
I'm sorry.

383
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:17,260
I know I've caused you guys trouble.

384
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:26,140
I'm

385
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:52,957
It's just a little better.

386
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,560
Just let's dance.

387
00:23:57,500 --> 00:23:59,600
Go up.

388
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:01,200
Look at him.

389
00:24:03,060 --> 00:24:04,640
Let's sit down.

390
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:06,793
Let's see what happens.

391
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:09,832
My patience will change.

392
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:12,397
There is a lot more power together.

393
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,310
Little love is strong.

394
00:24:13,393 --> 00:24:16,720
I'm so glad we all get this world.
